{"_comment": "Korax conformance fixture 10. Job ordering (§10.8, §12.7). Accepted log, in id order. `sig`/`board_sig` omitted; the generator fills them from conformance/keys.json. SHAPED AROUND ONE DISTINCTION: `part-of` is work breakdown and `gated-by` is ordering, and a board that conflates them passes a membership test and fails here. The campaign at 4-6 has an OPEN parent with two children; §12.7 makes any subset of the children claimable, so BOTH children are ready and neither is blocked. Read breakdown as blocked-by and `ready` holds only the parent — the reduction most wrong in the case the edge exists for. The gated chain at 7-8 is the other half, and offsets 12 and 14 pin the RELEASE: a closed blocker frees its dependent, a taken one does not."}
